{{also|Bronchitis}}
==English==
{{wp}}

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|LL.|bronchus}}, from {{af|en|grc:βρόγχος|t1=windpipe|-itis}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/bɹɒŋˈkaɪtɪs/|a=UK}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-bronchitis.wav|a=Southern England}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~|+|bronchitides}}

# {{lb|en|uncountable}} An [[inflammation]] of the [[bronchus|bronchi]] of the [[lung]]s, that causes the [[cilia]] of the bronchial epithelial cells to stop functioning.
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2015-11-17|author=|title=Single Pathogen Challenge with Agents of the Bovine Respiratory Disease Complex|journal=PLOS ONE|url=http://journals.plos.org/plosone/article?id=10.1371/journal.pone.0142479|doi=10.1371/journal.pone.0142479|volume=|issue=|pages=
|passage=Histological examination showed neutrophilic or pleocellular proliferative necrotizing '''bronchitis''' and bronchiolitis in all (6 out of 6) infected steers. }}
# {{lb|en|countable}} An occurrence of, a case (patient) of, or a type of bronchitis.

